Module7/NPCSimulator/python/venv/**

# The Python environment the Module 3 notebooks execute in.
# Rebuilt from pyproject.toml and uv.lock with `uv sync`, both of which are committed, so there is nothing here worth tracking.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/

# Quarto scratch and execution caches.
# .jupyter_cache is what stops a notebook's python running once per output format; _freeze is quarto's own, which only takes effect on a whole-project render.
# Neither is committed: both are derived from the .qmd and the locked environment.
**/.quarto/
Module3/.jupyter_cache/
Module3/_freeze/

# Rendered notebooks.
# The .qmd is the source and the .ipynb is the deliverable a student opens, so both of those are committed. The .html is a preview for whoever is authoring, and <stem>_files/ holds the figures and javascript it needs; Module3/render.sh regenerates them.
Module3/numericalCalculus_*.html
Module3/numericalCalculus_*_files/
